1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,678
Hi, I'm Edison Liu.

2
00:00:04,728 --> 00:00:09,572
I study electronic and computer
engineering at the ZJU-UIUC Institute.

3
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:15,652
I build working systems from start to
finish, from Arduino hardware to software.

4
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:20,694
AI agents are starting to
pay each other with x402.

5
00:00:20,744 --> 00:00:25,144
Once an x402 payment settles,
there is no chargeback.

6
00:00:25,194 --> 00:00:28,261
So agents mostly move small amounts.

7
00:00:28,311 --> 00:00:32,711
Tessera puts each payment
in an escrow on Solana.

8
00:00:32,761 --> 00:00:37,606
An on-chain credit score decides
how long the money waits.

9
00:00:37,656 --> 00:00:42,500
A fresh wallet waits. Two Trusted-tier
wallets can settle instantly.

10
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:50,020
The score comes only from orders that really
settled, so faking it costs real fees and time.

11
00:00:50,556 --> 00:00:58,746
Security research is my interest, so I started from
the threat model: who steals what, and at what cost.

12
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:02,517
I audited my own work twice.

13
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:11,477
The second time I found a critical bug: a merchant could
cancel and reopen an order to take a buyer’s payment.

14
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:17,194
I fixed it and wrote a test that proves it.

15
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:25,074
I build with Claude Code. I set the requirements
and the threat model, and I check the results.

16
00:01:25,694 --> 00:01:30,539
The code and the tests are
in the public repository.

17
00:01:30,589 --> 00:01:38,419
It runs on devnet with test money. There are
no outside users yet, and it is not audited.

18
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:45,429
Next, I want to talk to x402 sellers
who would charge more than cents.

19
00:01:45,711 --> 00:01:49,941
I intend to keep building it. Thank you.
